},
{
"level": "A2",
"el": "Ένα ποτήρι νερό",
"title": "Quantities, and adverbs with a genitive pronoun",
"body": [
{
"p": "**Quantities** do not take a genitive: the noun simply follows, in the same case as the measure."
},
{
"ex": [
{
"el": "ένα ποτήρι νερό",
"en": "a glass of water"
},
{
"el": "ένα κιλό ντομάτες",
"en": "a kilo of tomatoes"
},
{
"el": "ένα μπουκάλι κρασί",
"en": "a bottle of wine"
},
{
"el": "δύο φέτες ψωμί",
"en": "two slices of bread"
},
{
"el": "λίγο τυρί, πολλή ζάχαρη",
"en": "a little cheese, a lot of sugar"
}
]
},
{
"p": "**Adverbs of place** take **από** + noun or a genitive weak pronoun: **μπροστά από το σπίτι** \"in front of the house\" but **μπροστά μου** \"in front of me\"; **δίπλα στο περίπτερο** \"next to the kiosk\" but **δίπλα της** \"next to her\"."
},
{
